(1946807, 268119, 43463, '<td valign="top">A nice holiday spirit photo. Tones, lighting, and subject all all well captured. My one critique on strengthening the visual impact of the holiday spirit in the photo is that more of the christmas tree - as in the full trianglar shape could be present in the background. The candle would still be the main subject and should/can still retain the same size and porportion of the photo. By just moving the candle further away from the scene and composing the composition exactly as you did here more off and possibly the full tree would be visible in the background.</td>', 'A nice holiday spirit photo. Tones, lighting, and subject all all well captured. My one critique on strengthening the visual impact of the holiday spirit in the photo is that more of the christmas tree - as in the full trianglar shape could be present in the background. The candle would still be the main subject and should/can still retain the same size and porportion of the photo. By just moving the candle further away from the scene and composing the composition exactly as you did here more off and possibly the full tree would be visible in the background.', '2005-12-13 10:54:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946808, 267186, 47117, '<td valign="top">I prefer to not only see candles in a candlelight challenge, but I don''t care to see human subjects in it.  I tend to believe that human models "can" give away anonymity at times, unless only the backs of heads are shown and things along those lines.  The lighting is nice, but could be from any low light source. Without the candle, and with the head on model portrait, I voted this way down. Sorry.</td>', 'I prefer to not only see candles in a candlelight challenge, but I don''t care to see human subjects in it.  I tend to believe that human models "can" give away anonymity at times, unless only the backs of heads are shown and things along those lines.  The lighting is nice, but could be from any low light source. Without the candle, and with the head on model portrait, I voted this way down. Sorry.', '2005-12-13 10:54:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946819, 268299, 47117, '<td valign="top">Quite frankly, I am tired of breast shots. LOL...I really don''t see need for it here, and even your title doesn''t really represent anything sensual about this shot. She is merely holding the candle, very contrived, on top of her chest and blatently looking at the camera, giving this a less candid feel and appeal.  Maybe had she been wearing a sexy bra or something, it may have given more to the mystique side of the shot. Had the wax been seen dripping on her chest it may also have added, but to me? This is nothing more than an excuse to show nudity, and it is well seen that nude photos on this site have the most clicks given to them. I voted this very low.</td>', 'Quite frankly, I am tired of breast shots. LOL...I really don''t see need for it here, and even your title doesn''t really represent anything sensual about this shot. She is merely holding the candle, very contrived, on top of her chest and blatently looking at the camera, giving this a less candid feel and appeal.  Maybe had she been wearing a sexy bra or something, it may have given more to the mystique side of the shot. Had the wax been seen dripping on her chest it may also have added, but to me? This is nothing more than an excuse to show nudity, and it is well seen that nude photos on this site have the most clicks given to them. I voted this very low.', '2005-12-13 10:59:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946822, 266570, 47117, '<td valign="top">Very sweet, but also very blurred and I don''t see any candles.  I see what could be any type of low light. Candlelight is hard to take shots of. I wish you would have given it a try.  I voted this way down, sorry.</td>', 'Very sweet, but also very blurred and I don''t see any candles.  I see what could be any type of low light. Candlelight is hard to take shots of. I wish you would have given it a try.  I voted this way down, sorry.', '2005-12-13 11:00:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946823, 268218, 47117, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, but the candlelight is lacking, or should I say the candle. Had the candle been visible, I would have voted this a bit higher,but I voted this very low due to the cause of the light being any kind of low light source.  Candlelight is hard to take shots of. I wish you would have shown us your try at the flame.</td>', 'Nice idea, but the candlelight is lacking, or should I say the candle. Had the candle been visible, I would have voted this a bit higher,but I voted this very low due to the cause of the light being any kind of low light source.  Candlelight is hard to take shots of. I wish you would have shown us your try at the flame.', '2005-12-13 11:02:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946827, 266870, 43463, '<td valign="top">The only thing lacking in this festive holiday card photo are those nice warm tones that are cast on the whole scene by the glow of the candlelights. The lighting here is a full on white light either from daylight lighting the scene or by indoor lighting. There are none of those nice warm orange/yellow tones that bath the scene in a warm and inviting light. It is that type of light (candlelight) that could help the scene become more warm in mood and feeling.</td>', 'The only thing lacking in this festive holiday card photo are those nice warm tones that are cast on the whole scene by the glow of the candlelights. The lighting here is a full on white light either from daylight lighting the scene or by indoor lighting. There are none of those nice warm orange/yellow tones that bath the scene in a warm and inviting light. It is that type of light (candlelight) that could help the scene become more warm in mood and feeling.', '2005-12-13 11:03:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946838, 267483, 47124, '<td valign="top">i like it</td>', 'i like it', '2005-12-13 11:07:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946839, 266891, 47117, '<td valign="top">This photo is extremely small, and it may have been your sizing factor that distorted the image so much.  It is FULL of noise, and blur, and its too bad because it looks like you got a really nice star effect to the flame.  Unfortunately, I had to vote this my lowest of a one for very bad composition and size.</td>', 'This photo is extremely small, and it may have been your sizing factor that distorted the image so much.  It is FULL of noise, and blur, and its too bad because it looks like you got a really nice star effect to the flame.  Unfortunately, I had to vote this my lowest of a one for very bad composition and size.', '2005-12-13 11:08:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946842, 267045, 47117, '<td valign="top">At first I voted this a 2.  I could not see any candlelight here and a lot of, basically, unfocused material. But because I ''think" I see what may be a flame in the actual base of teh shot (that little blue light), or maybe the wick...LOL.not sure, I am going to bump it up one notch for that.  It''s a pretty thing, but the shot just lacks for me.</td>', 'At first I voted this a 2.  I could not see any candlelight here and a lot of, basically, unfocused material. But because I ''think" I see what may be a flame in the actual base of teh shot (that little blue light), or maybe the wick...LOL.not sure, I am going to bump it up one notch for that.  It''s a pretty thing, but the shot just lacks for me.', '2005-12-13 11:10:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946845, 266570, 43463, '<td valign="top">Tis a shame the the photo is blurred and fuzzy for I see all those nice warm orange/yellow tones that really complement the skin tones of the people in this shot. A sharper more detailed image would be better. Either the subjects needed to be more still for the long exposure on the camera or you might have introduced another light source (a few more candles off screne to help with exposure time. Also pulling back and not having such a tight crop on the two people to show more of just a head shot (full head from the neck up) would be better visually. It could also add to the composition possibly if you included a burning candle in the shot that would rest just below the faces and between them so as to not obscure the people. The symbology woutd be to strengthen the visual imagery of ''burning/heated passion both in the kiss being exchanged and the burning flame.</td>', 'Tis a shame the the photo is blurred and fuzzy for I see all those nice warm orange/yellow tones that really complement the skin tones of the people in this shot. A sharper more detailed image would be better. Either the subjects needed to be more still for the long exposure on the camera or you might have introduced another light source (a few more candles off screne to help with exposure time. Also pulling back and not having such a tight crop on the two people to show more of just a head shot (full head from the neck up) would be better visually. It could also add to the composition possibly if you included a burning candle in the shot that would rest just below the faces and between them so as to not obscure the people. The symbology woutd be to strengthen the visual imagery of ''burning/heated passion both in the kiss being exchanged and the burning flame.', '2005-12-13 11:11:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946846, 267825, 47117, '<td valign="top">Pretty girl, without the fangs, but I would have to say that I like to see candle flame in a contest such as "Candlelight". This could really be any low light source, or even manipulated light sourcing.  I voted this way down for not showing what you could as for the actual flame.</td>', 'Pretty girl, without the fangs, but I would have to say that I like to see candle flame in a contest such as "Candlelight". This could really be any low light source, or even manipulated light sourcing.  I voted this way down for not showing what you could as for the actual flame.', '2005-12-13 11:11:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946849, 266189, 47117, '<td valign="top">And the candlelight is where? Did you enter the wrong challenge?  I find this not to meet the challenge, and I don''t give scores that are high for shots that don''t, even if the rules say you shouldn''t vote them low if they don''t meet challenge.  Unfortunately, a lot of people tried very hard to take what is a difficult shot of a flame, and yours is a landscape/seascape shot.  It''s very pretty, but just perplexing to see it here in this challenge.  I voted this very low. Sorry.</td>', 'And the candlelight is where? Did you enter the wrong challenge?  I find this not to meet the challenge, and I don''t give scores that are high for shots that don''t, even if the rules say you shouldn''t vote them low if they don''t meet challenge.  Unfortunately, a lot of people tried very hard to take what is a difficult shot of a flame, and yours is a landscape/seascape shot.  It''s very pretty, but just perplexing to see it here in this challenge.  I voted this very low. Sorry.', '2005-12-13 11:13:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946870, 267682, 43463, '<td valign="top">Love the warm tones thrown off from the candlelight that really complement the skin tones of the model. Her pose and facial features help project the mood of quiet contemplation. Photo is technically well exposed with details sharply and cleary shown in the fur jacket, a well defined candle flame  and even down to the sheen on her lips. My only critique on this photo is that I would have liked to have seen her hands holding the candle. If the models hands are "cradling" or gently clasping the candle between her hands it would strengthen the mood of ''quiet contemplation''.</td>', 'Love the warm tones thrown off from the candlelight that really complement the skin tones of the model. Her pose and facial features help project the mood of quiet contemplation. Photo is technically well exposed with details sharply and cleary shown in the fur jacket, a well defined candle flame  and even down to the sheen on her lips. My only critique on this photo is that I would have liked to have seen her hands holding the candle. If the models hands are "cradling" or gently clasping the candle between her hands it would strengthen the mood of ''quiet contemplation''.', '2005-12-13 11:21:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946895, 267569, 43463, '<td valign="top">This is an photo of interest in regards to photojournalism -documenting events. My critique is that the scene is way to busy as that there are tooooo many elements present that the eye does not have a main subject dominating the scene for us to train our attention on. There are numerous photos of John Lennon, flowers, candles a person''s pants and elbow visible on the left hand side, a camera visible on the right hand side, etc. It comes off too much like a quick snapshot. Training the composition to focus on a few objects in the scene would greatly strengthen the visual and emotional impact of the photo - say a tighter focus on John Lennon''s face on the center and the words imagine is one suggestion. Another is if you were positioned at a different angle such that when that person in the background was placing that lighted candle down next to the words "Imagine" would be another (visually and emotionally this would be a great photo for it says in a visual message that his words and hope for a better world has not died out - the flame still burns brightly as does his memory)</td>', 'This is an photo of interest in regards to photojournalism -documenting events. My critique is that the scene is way to busy as that there are tooooo many elements present that the eye does not have a main subject dominating the scene for us to train our attention on. There are numerous photos of John Lennon, flowers, candles a person''s pants and elbow visible on the left hand side, a camera visible on the right hand side, etc. It comes off too much like a quick snapshot. Training the composition to focus on a few objects in the scene would greatly strengthen the visual and emotional impact of the photo - say a tighter focus on John Lennon''s face on the center and the words imagine is one suggestion. Another is if you were positioned at a different angle such that when that person in the background was placing that lighted candle down next to the words "Imagine" would be another (visually and emotionally this would be a great photo for it says in a visual message that his words and hope for a better world has not died out - the flame still burns brightly as does his memory)', '2005-12-13 11:31:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946956, 268055, 7743, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea.  The objects, candle, slinky and shadow, are nicely position within the frame.  The colour is very calming though the flame appears to be blown out.<br/></td>', 'Interesting idea.  The objects, candle, slinky and shadow, are nicely position within the frame.  The colour is very calming though the flame appears to be blown out.', '2005-12-13 11:58:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946959, 268274, 22379, '<td valign="top">The photoshopping effects used onthis image is undesirable for a photography competition. This is more in the realm of digital art.</td>', 'The photoshopping effects used onthis image is undesirable for a photography competition. This is more in the realm of digital art.', '2005-12-13 11:58:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946961, 266280, 7743, '<td valign="top">The objects are nicely arranged within the frame however the OOF flame which seems to be blown out is quite distracting.  It is the brightest part of the image where the eye is generally drawn.</td>', 'The objects are nicely arranged within the frame however the OOF flame which seems to be blown out is quite distracting.  It is the brightest part of the image where the eye is generally drawn.', '2005-12-13 11:59:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946968, 266570, 22379, '<td valign="top">This is an out of focus, blurry image. I can only assume tghat the photogrpaher has some sentiment attached to the image. When choosing an image for a challenge, it is important to consider "do i believe this photo is good it has visual and technical appeal to an ignorant (nmeaning someone with no infrmation on the subject) viewer, or do i think it is good because i am emotionally attached to it". Entering images you are emotionally attached to can be quite disappointing as  the voter will not escuse the flaws as you do.</td>', 'This is an out of focus, blurry image. I can only assume tghat the photogrpaher has some sentiment attached to the image. When choosing an image for a challenge, it is important to consider "do i believe this photo is good it has visual and technical appeal to an ignorant (nmeaning someone with no infrmation on the subject) viewer, or do i think it is good because i am emotionally attached to it". Entering images you are emotionally attached to can be quite disappointing as  the voter will not escuse the flaws as you do.', '2005-12-13 12:02:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946979, 267682, 49102, '<td valign="top">Beautiful lighting of the face, good composition and good clearness.</td>', 'Beautiful lighting of the face, good composition and good clearness.', '2005-12-13 12:07:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946981, 267537, 22379, '<td valign="top">The scene is pleasant but ruined buy the blobish looking towls in the front of the frame. There is no real subject in the image. <br/>It would have been stronger if you had allowed the horizonal lines in the image (ie the tiles) to run paallel with the frame of the image. The angle you have choses ismore "snapshotish" and lends itself to distractions like the dark edge of the bath. Allowing the candles to starburse rather than just be white blurs would have given an richer effect to the lighting.</td>', 'The scene is pleasant but ruined buy the blobish looking towls in the front of the frame. There is no real subject in the image. It would have been stronger if you had allowed the horizonal lines in the image (ie the tiles) to run paallel with the frame of the image. The angle you have choses ismore "snapshotish" and lends itself to distractions like the dark edge of the bath. Allowing the candles to starburse rather than just be white blurs would have given an richer effect to the lighting.', '2005-12-13 12:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946985, 267947, 49102, '<td valign="top">Put on page which questions, very beautiful liminosity and beautiful reflections.</td>', 'Put on page which questions, very beautiful liminosity and beautiful reflections.', '2005-12-13 12:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946990, 267680, 49102, '<td valign="top">composition in diagonal, soft lighting, good luminosity</td>', 'composition in diagonal, soft lighting, good luminosity', '2005-12-13 12:11:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1946995, 267670, 49102, '<td valign="top">good composition, the candle is on a main line, beautiful coloris.Image unbalanced a little</td>', 'good composition, the candle is on a main line, beautiful coloris.Image unbalanced a little', '2005-12-13 12:14:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1947002, 267312, 49102, '<td valign="top">A beautiful test to photograph a flame but I think that a little clearness would have given more broadth to the subject.</td>', 'A beautiful test to photograph a flame but I think that a little clearness would have given more broadth to the subject.', '2005-12-13 12:17:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1947007, 267762, 32767, '<td valign="top">Best In Show. Good Luck! My only 10 vote in the Challenge (after my own image ...of course).<br/> <br/>...and I think...I''d bet almost anything that I know who took this image.</td>', 'Best In Show. Good Luck! My only 10 vote in the Challenge (after my own image ...of course). ...and I think...I''d bet almost anything that I know who took this image.', '2005-12-13 12:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
