(1969979, 267049, 37544, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by macrothing:</b></div><hr/><i> 6 - Met the Challenge quite well in my opinion - <i> "Use candlelight to create the impact of your photo."</i>.  Criticism; whilst I like the concept (including use of color/pink(s)), this has more potential in my opinion. edit:removed ''unhelpful comments'', sorry you did not find my comments helpful </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Don''t take it personal, I just really had no idea of what you were talking about.</td>', 'Originally posted by macrothing: 6 - Met the Challenge quite well in my opinion -  "Use candlelight to create the impact of your photo.".  Criticism; whilst I like the concept (including use of color/pink(s)), this has more potential in my opinion. edit:removed ''unhelpful comments'', sorry you did not find my comments helpful   Don''t take it personal, I just really had no idea of what you were talking about.', '2005-12-22 00:14:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1969995, 267666, 48560, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 9. Seeing how smart the idea and execution is, I now traced the photo to it''s owner, and voila - it''s you again Robt! I personally think it''s a good one. Maybe if the bowl and stuff could be more symmetrical on the vertical, it would be much better. Just my opinion.</td>', 'I gave this a 9. Seeing how smart the idea and execution is, I now traced the photo to it''s owner, and voila - it''s you again Robt! I personally think it''s a good one. Maybe if the bowl and stuff could be more symmetrical on the vertical, it would be much better. Just my opinion.', '2005-12-22 00:17:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1970044, 268053, 46448, '<td valign="top">I see the problem it lacks cowbell! No really every thing is on for this shot But it just three candles burning, 5.7 isn''t that bad.. it just didn''t have the pop to have enough to keep intrest...</td>', 'I see the problem it lacks cowbell! No really every thing is on for this shot But it just three candles burning, 5.7 isn''t that bad.. it just didn''t have the pop to have enough to keep intrest...', '2005-12-22 00:36:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1970848, 266189, 14476, '<td valign="top">Comment: <br/>Greetings from the Critique Club <br/> <br/>Hello, moonjeong! How lucky I am to get to look at another of your images for the Critique Club. <br/> <br/>Your image is just lovely, with good composition and a nice mood. Did you use a tripod? I think it would have helped this very nice photograph if it was just a little sharper and a tripod is good for that under difficult lighting conditions. Then, with a tripod, you could experiment with using a lower ISO to make it even more colorful. <br/> <br/>I guess people were looking for literal candles providing "candlelight" rather than the quotation you offered. That may be why your score is not higher! <br/> <br/>I hope you are pleased with this image. It is a nice one.</td>', 'Comment: Greetings from the Critique Club  Hello, moonjeong! How lucky I am to get to look at another of your images for the Critique Club.  Your image is just lovely, with good composition and a nice mood. Did you use a tripod? I think it would have helped this very nice photograph if it was just a little sharper and a tripod is good for that under difficult lighting conditions. Then, with a tripod, you could experiment with using a lower ISO to make it even more colorful.  I guess people were looking for literal candles providing "candlelight" rather than the quotation you offered. That may be why your score is not higher!  I hope you are pleased with this image. It is a nice one.', '2005-12-22 09:58:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1972005, 268053, 40718, '<td valign="top">another one I liked.  I gave this a 7.  Composition is nice with off centered image and good, but not too much, negative space.  I like the star effect and don''t think it dominates too much.  There are a few pixels of white which could easily be removed with a mild run through "despeckle" in PS.  Perhaps just a tad overexposed with the flames, but this was a demanding challenge and there were many which were worse.</td>', 'another one I liked.  I gave this a 7.  Composition is nice with off centered image and good, but not too much, negative space.  I like the star effect and don''t think it dominates too much.  There are a few pixels of white which could easily be removed with a mild run through "despeckle" in PS.  Perhaps just a tad overexposed with the flames, but this was a demanding challenge and there were many which were worse.', '2005-12-22 18:42:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973017, 265718, 22734, '<td valign="top">A very nice image but with the short span time that voters spend, the beauty of it will be missed by many.</td>', 'A very nice image but with the short span time that voters spend, the beauty of it will be missed by many.', '2005-12-23 00:42:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973182, 268055, 17507, '<td valign="top">I knew you had to ribbon sooner or later - you''re just too creative to escape DPC''s front page! Congratulations and well-earned! I love a picture that doesn''t take itself too seriously yet is uncompromisingly excellent.</td>', 'I knew you had to ribbon sooner or later - you''re just too creative to escape DPC''s front page! Congratulations and well-earned! I love a picture that doesn''t take itself too seriously yet is uncompromisingly excellent.', '2005-12-23 01:50:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973345, 268119, 4226, '<td valign="top">**Critique Club** <br/>The first thing that I see here is the candle light and its yellow and warm, nice exposed flame and you have chosen an apt title for the image too. <br/> <br/>Looking at the details you provided, an aperture 25 was used, I would assume you wanted a deep dof to keep most of the things in focus, but the background at this moment is quiet soft. Were you too close to the candle ? Also write down the lens used as this may help. <br/> <br/>You could have possibly used a bit more for the background. the left side at present is quiet dull and could use some lights in the background to balance the image. <br/> <br/>if you have any questions, please feel free to pm me <br/>Gaurawa <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by HBunch - Fixed CC glitch.</i></td>', '**Critique Club** The first thing that I see here is the candle light and its yellow and warm, nice exposed flame and you have chosen an apt title for the image too.  Looking at the details you provided, an aperture 25 was used, I would assume you wanted a deep dof to keep most of the things in focus, but the background at this moment is quiet soft. Were you too close to the candle ? Also write down the lens used as this may help.  You could have possibly used a bit more for the background. the left side at present is quiet dull and could use some lights in the background to balance the image.  if you have any questions, please feel free to pm me Gaurawa Message edited by HBunch - Fixed CC glitch.', '2005-12-23 05:58:54.000000', NULL, 0),
