(3116984, 267871, 66635, '<td valign="top">Ok, now I''m still quite the novice at photography.  But, it says that the ISO was 100 and the shutter speed was 1 second.  How is an ISO of 100 fast enough to perfectly expose a bullet that is traveling at somewhere near 2,000 feet per second?  Second, how is it that, on the left side of the screen, the bullet stayed in one spot long enough for a perfect exposure, whereas on the rest of the screen it was just a blur?  It''s a cool picture; but I don''t think it''s really a stopped-motion picture of a bullet in flight.</td>', 'Ok, now I''m still quite the novice at photography.  But, it says that the ISO was 100 and the shutter speed was 1 second.  How is an ISO of 100 fast enough to perfectly expose a bullet that is traveling at somewhere near 2,000 feet per second?  Second, how is it that, on the left side of the screen, the bullet stayed in one spot long enough for a perfect exposure, whereas on the rest of the screen it was just a blur?  It''s a cool picture; but I don''t think it''s really a stopped-motion picture of a bullet in flight.', '2006-12-14 11:22:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3145990, 268221, 47721, '<td valign="top">Hey Rachel,<br/> <br/>Love this picture... very warm and cosy......beautiful lighting... feels like a place I''d like to be...</td>', 'Hey Rachel, Love this picture... very warm and cosy......beautiful lighting... feels like a place I''d like to be...', '2006-12-24 08:51:56.000000', NULL, 0),
